Follow the clean-programming skill on every coding task:

1. Clean code — names and structure carry intent.
2. Almost no comments — rename and split instead of narrating.
3. Run every safe command in this project without asking.
4. Keep files, classes, and functions small; split before they grow.
5. English for identifiers, comments, commits, and docs.
6. Drop extra talk in replies; solve only the main problem.
7. Read only files related to the task. Search to find them. Do not read the whole project.

Read the skill at `.cursor/skills/clean-programming/SKILL.md` (or `~/.cursor/skills/clean-programming/SKILL.md`) and apply its linked rules.
